---
/* What is measured, in plain words.
 *
 * Every claim on this page is a claim about code in this repository, and the
 * code is named so it can be checked rather than believed. A privacy page that
 * describes an intention rather than an implementation is the same failure as
 * a config file that validates and does nothing.
 */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE_NAME } from "../lib/config";
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy — ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description="What this site measures, what it does not, and how to stop it."
>
  <header class="top no-print">
    <a class="home" href="/">{SITE_NAME}</a>
  </header>

  <main class="article">
    <div class="masthead">
      <h1>What this site measures</h1>
      <p class="dek">
        Short version: a random number in your browser, which pages you looked at, and how
        far down you got. No third parties, no advertising, and nothing that identifies you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>What is recorded</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>A random identifier</strong> this site generates and keeps in your browser's
        local storage. It is not derived from anything about you — it identifies a browser, not
        a person, and clearing site data genuinely resets it.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Which pages you opened</strong>, how far you scrolled, roughly how long the tab
        was actually visible, and whether you clicked through to the research portal.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Where you arrived from</strong> — the referring site and any campaign tags on
        the link — recorded once, on your first visit.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>A two-letter country</strong>, worked out at the network edge, and a coarse
        device class (phone, tablet or desktop) based on window width.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is not</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your IP address.</strong> The country is resolved before the request reaches our
        code, and the address itself is never written down. It is not stored anywhere.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Your user-agent string</strong>, or any browser or device fingerprint.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Anything a third party set.</strong> There are no third-party cookies, no
        advertising pixels and no external analytics. Nothing on a report page makes a request
        to anyone but us.
      </li>
      <li><strong>Your name or email</strong>, unless you type one into the form below a report.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How to stop it</h2>
    <p>
      Turn on <strong>Do Not Track</strong> or <strong>Global Privacy Control</strong> in your
      browser. This site checks for both <em>before</em> it generates an identifier or touches
      storage — so with either set you are not merely un-reported, you are un-recorded. Clearing
      site data removes the identifier and the next visit starts a new one.
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      Entirely optional, and nothing on this site is behind it. Every report is free to read
      whether or not you sign up. If you tick the consent box we record that you agreed to be
      emailed; if you do not, the address is stored with consent recorded as false and nothing
      is sent. We also record which report you signed up from, so we know which work was worth
      reading.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we measure at all</h2>
    <p>
      This site is free and is meant to be found. Knowing which reports get read, and how far,
      is how we decide what to write next — which is a better arrangement for a reader than
      putting the work behind a signup form and measuring that instead.
    </p>

    <p class="fine">
      Anonymous first-party measurement is processed on the basis of legitimate interest; the
      optional email is consent. If you want the identifier or an address removed, ask and it
      will be.
    </p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to the site</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .top {
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 14px 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .home {
    font-weight: 640;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .article {
    padding: 34px 0 72px;
  }
  .masthead {
    display: grid;
    gap: 9px;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(27px, 1.6rem + 1.8vw, 40px);
    line-height: 1.13;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    font-weight: 660;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .dek {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1rem + 0.3vw, 18px);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--body);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }
  h2 {
    margin: 30px 0 8px;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 640;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
    display: grid;
    gap: 7px;
  }
  li,
  p {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .article > p {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }
  strong {
    font-weight: 650;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .fine {
    margin-top: 28px;
    padding-top: 14px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hair);
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--small);
  }
  .back {
    margin-top: 22px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
  }
</style>
